From: jt914 <josephtso914@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Keep no security codes by default

Chrome keeps a card's security code with the card by default and says so
in its save bubble. EngineCore's embedder offers the save in a one-line
prompt with no room to say it, and a stored code makes the saved card a
complete card-not-present credential, so the code would be kept silently.
The "Save security codes" setting now defaults to off. With it off, a
saved card's code is cleared and no code-only offer is made; the switch on
the Payment methods page turns it back on.
---
diff --git a/components/autofill/core/common/autofill_prefs.cc b/components/autofill/core/common/autofill_prefs.cc
--- a/components/autofill/core/common/autofill_prefs.cc
+++ b/components/autofill/core/common/autofill_prefs.cc
@@ -75,8 +75,10 @@ void RegisterProfilePrefs(user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable* registry) {
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
       kAutofillCreditCardEnabled, true,
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
+  // EngineCore keeps no security code unless the user turns this on: its
+  // save prompt has no room to say it would keep one.
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
-      kAutofillPaymentCvcStorage, true,
+      kAutofillPaymentCvcStorage, false,
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
       kAutofillPaymentCardBenefits, true,
